
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Computer Science Ethics</title>
<style>
body{margin:0;padding:25px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background:#f2fbf4;color:#24452d}
header{text-align:center;background:#347a4b;color:white;padding:30px;border-radius:18px}
main{max-width:820px;margin:25px auto}
.rule{background:white;padding:21px;margin:15px 0;border-radius:13px;border-left:6px solid #62a873}
h2{color:#347a4b}
footer{text-align:center;background:#dff3e3;padding:18px;border-radius:12px}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header><h1>⚖️ Computer Science Ethics</h1><p>Use technology responsibly and fairly.</p></header>
<main>
<article class="rule"><h2>1. Respect Privacy</h2><p>Collect and share personal data responsibly, and respect people's consent.</p></article>
<article class="rule"><h2>2. Respect Copyright</h2><p>Give credit to creators and follow the licenses for code, images and other resources.</p></article>
<article class="rule"><h2>3. Be Honest</h2><p>Present your own work truthfully and acknowledge contributions from others.</p></article>
<article class="rule"><h2>4. Avoid Harm</h2><p>Build and use technology in ways that reduce harm to people and communities.</p></article>
<article class="rule"><h2>5. Design for Fairness</h2><p>Consider accessibility and different users' needs when creating digital products.</p></article>
<article class="rule"><h2>6. Protect Information</h2><p>Use appropriate security practices to protect accounts, devices and data.</p></article>
<footer><h2>💚 Think Before You Code</h2><p>Good technology should be useful, safe and responsible.</p></footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
